<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="text-transform: uppercase"><B>Amendment
No. 1 </B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="text-transform: uppercase"><B>to AMENDED
AND RESTATED</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="text-transform: uppercase"><B>Membership
interest purchase AGREEMENT</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">This Amendment No. 1 (this
&ldquo;<U>Amendment</U>&rdquo;) dated November 14, 2023 (the &ldquo;<U>Amendment Effective Date</U>&rdquo; to Amended and Restated Membership
Interest Purchase Agreement, dated as of August 28, 2023, is made by and among <B>CIC Pogo LP</B>, a Delaware limited partnership (&ldquo;<U>CIC</U>&rdquo;),
<B>DenCo Resources, LLC</B>, a Texas limited liability company (&ldquo;<U>DenCo</U>&rdquo;), <B>Pogo Resources Management, LLC</B>, a
Texas limited liability company (&ldquo;<U>Pogo Management</U>&rdquo;), <B>4400 Holdings, LLC, </B>a Texas limited liability company (&ldquo;<U>4400</U>&rdquo;
and, together with CIC, DenCo and Pogo Management, collectively, &ldquo;<U>Seller</U>&rdquo; and each a &ldquo;<U>Seller</U>&rdquo;),
<B>HNR Acquisition Corp</B>, a Delaware corporation (&ldquo;<U>HNRA</U>&rdquo; or the &ldquo;<U>SPAC</U>&rdquo;), <B>HNRA PARTNER, INC.</B>,
a Delaware corporation, (&ldquo;<U>SPAC Subsidiary</U>&rdquo;), <B>HNRA UPSTREAM, LLC</B>, a Delaware limited liability company (&ldquo;<U>OpCo</U>&rdquo;,
and together with HNRA, SPAC Subsidiary and &ldquo;<U>Buyer</U>&rdquo; and each a &ldquo;<U>Buyer</U>&rdquo;) and, solely with respect
to <FONT STYLE="font-weight: normal"><U>&lrm;</U></FONT><U>Section 6.20</U>, <B>HNRAC Sponsors LLC</B>, a Delaware limited liability company
(&ldquo;<B>Sponsor</B>&rdquo;). Seller and Buyer may hereafter be referred to each as a &ldquo;<U>Party</U>&rdquo; and together as the
&ldquo;<U>Parties</U>.&rdquo; Capitalized terms used herein but not otherwise defined have the respectively meanings attributed to them
in the MIPA (defined below).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="text-transform: uppercase"><B>Recitals</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="text-transform: uppercase"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="text-transform: uppercase"><B>Whereas</B></FONT>,
Seller, Buyer, and, solely with respect to Section 6.20 therein,&nbsp;Sponsor, are parties to that certain Amended and Restated Membership
Interest Purchase Agreement, dated as of August 28, 2023 (the &ldquo;<U>MIPA</U>&rdquo;); and</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><B>WHEREAS</B>, pursuant to
Section 11.6 of the MIPA, the MIPA may be amended by a written agreement duly executed by each of the Parties thereto; and</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><B>WHEREAS</B>, Buyer and
Seller desire to enter into this Amendment in order to amend the MIPA in the manner set forth herein.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="text-transform: uppercase"><B>Now,
Therefore</B></FONT>, in consideration of the representations, warranties, covenants and agreements herein made and for other good and
valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which are hereby acknowledged, the parties hereto agree as follows:</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="text-transform: uppercase"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="text-transform: uppercase"><B>Agreement</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">1.<FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;
</FONT><B><U>Amendment to MIPA</U></B>. The MIPA is hereby amended as follows:</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" WIDTH="100%" STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><TR STYLE="vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="width: 0.5in"></TD><TD STYLE="width: 0.25in">(a)</TD><TD STYLE="text-align: justify">The definition of &ldquo;Option Agreement&rdquo; in Section 1.1 of the MIPA is hereby amended and restated
in its entirety as follow:</TD></TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 1in; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 1in; text-align: justify">&ldquo;&ldquo;<U>Option Agreement</U>&rdquo;
means that option agreement by and between Pogo Royalty, LLC (an Affiliate of Seller) and HNRA Royalties LLC (an Affiliate of Buyer) in
the form attached hereto as <U>Exhibit C</U>.&rdquo;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.75in; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.75in; text-align: justify"></P>

<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 1; Options: NewSection; Value: 1 -->
    <DIV STYLE="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1.5pt solid"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <DIV STYLE="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <!-- Field: /Page -->

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.75in; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" WIDTH="100%" STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><TR STYLE="vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="width: 0.5in"></TD><TD STYLE="width: 0.25in">(b)</TD><TD STYLE="text-align: justify">Section 2.2 of the MIPA is hereby amended and restated in its entirety as follows:</TD></TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 1in; text-align: justify">&ldquo;Section 2.2 <U>Aggregate Consideration</U>.
The aggregate consideration for the Target Interests shall be (a), cash in the amount of $63,000,000 in immediately available funds (the
&ldquo;<U>Cash Consideration</U>&rdquo;), (b) 2,000,000 units of OpCo Class B Units valued at $10.00 per unit (the &ldquo;<U>Common Unit
Consideration</U>&rdquo;), which shall be equal to 2,000,000 shares of SPAC Class A Common Stock issuable upon exercise of the OpCo Holder
Redemption Right, as reflected in the A&amp;R OpCo LLC Agreement and (c) and the Seller Class B Shares; provided, that (i) a portion of
the Cash Consideration not to exceed $15,000,000 may be payable through the Promissory Note to Seller to the extent the Minimum Cash Amount
is less than $63,000,000 and (ii) a portion of the Cash Consideration not to exceed $20,000,000 may be payable through the issuance of
up to 2,000,000 units of OpCo Preferred Units (the &ldquo;<U>Preferred Unit Consideration</U>&rdquo;, and, together with the Common Unit
Consideration, the &ldquo;<U>Unit Consideration</U>&rdquo;), to the extent the Minimum Cash Amount is less than $48,000,000. At Closing,
500,000 shares of the Seller Class B Shares (the &ldquo;<U>Escrowed Share Consideration</U>&rdquo;) shall be placed in escrow with the
Escrow Agent for the benefit of Buyer pursuant to the Escrow Agreement and the indemnity provisions herein. The Unit Consideration and
Escrowed Share Consideration shall be proportionately adjusted to reflect any stock split, combination of shares, stock dividend, reorganization,
recapitalization or other similar event affecting the SPAC Common Stock, the OpCo Class B Units, the Seller Class B Shares or the OpCo
Preferred Units occurring after the date of this Agreement and prior to the Closing so as to provide Seller the same economic effect as
contemplated by this Agreement prior to such change.&rdquo;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" WIDTH="100%" STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><TR STYLE="vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="width: 0.5in"></TD><TD STYLE="width: 0.25in">(c)</TD><TD STYLE="text-align: justify">All instances of the defined term &ldquo;Escrowed Unit Consideration&rdquo; are hereby replaced with &ldquo;Escrowed
Share Consideration&rdquo;.</TD></TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.75in; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" WIDTH="100%" STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><TR STYLE="vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="width: 0.5in"></TD><TD STYLE="width: 0.25in">(d)</TD><TD STYLE="text-align: justify">Section 9.1(b) of the MIPA is hereby amended and restated in its entirety as follows:</TD></TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.75in; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 1in; text-align: justify">&ldquo;(b) by Seller or Buyer if Closing
has not occurred on or before November 30, 2023 (the &ldquo;<U>Outside Date</U>&rdquo;);&rdquo;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 1in; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" WIDTH="100%" STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><TR STYLE="vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="width: 0.5in"></TD><TD STYLE="width: 0.25in">(e)</TD><TD STYLE="text-align: justify">Section 10.4(b)(3) of the MIPA is hereby amended and restated in its entirety as follows:</TD></TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.75in; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 1in; text-align: justify">&ldquo;(3) In no event shall any Sellers
aggregate liability to Buyer and Buyer Indemnitees under Section 10.2(a)(1) exceed the value of the Escrowed Share Consideration, except
in the case of breaches of the Seller Fundamental Representations or in the case of actual Fraud; and&rdquo;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 1in; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">2. &nbsp;<B><U>Effect
on the MIPA</U></B>. Except as specifically amended by this Amendment, the MIPA shall remain in full force and effect, and the MIPA, as
amended by this Amendment, is hereby ratified and confirmed in all respects. From and after the Amendment Effective Date, each reference
in the MIPA to &ldquo;this Agreement,&rdquo; &ldquo;herein,&rdquo; &ldquo;hereof,&rdquo; &ldquo;hereunder&rdquo; or words of similar import,
or to any provision of the MIPA, as the case may be, shall be deemed to refer to the MIPA or such provision as amended by this Amendment,
unless the context otherwise requires.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">3. &nbsp;<B><U>Miscellaneous</U></B>.
The provisions of Sections 11.1 (Counterparts), 11.2 (Notices), 11.4 (Law; Venue), 11.5 (Jurisdiction; Waiver of Jury Trial), 11.6 (Amendment;
Waivers), 11.7 (Assignment), 11.8 (Entire Agreement), 11.9 (No Third Party Beneficiaries), 11.10 (Invalid Provisions), 11.11 (Construction),
11.12 (Limitation on Damages), and 11.13 (No Recourse), of the MIPA are incorporated by reference into this Amendment <I>mutatis mutandis</I>.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center">[<I>Remainder of Page Intentionally Left Blank;
Signature Pages Follow</I>]</P>

